OSKit RS — Restart Server (userspace)
======================================

Minix 3-style service manager. Runs as the first userspace
process — the kernel loads RS from a boot module, then RS
loads all other servers and init.

RS reads its configuration from an info page at 0xBF000
written by the kernel before RS starts:
  +0:  RS TID (unused — RS sets its own)
  +8:  ramdisk base physical address (i64)
  +16: ramdisk size (i64)
  +24: boot info header copy (SLIX magic + module entries)

Boot module data lives in physical memory. RS uses
svc_phys_read to copy it into its own address space.

Boot order:
1. Disk server (no dependencies)
2. TFS server (depends on disk)
3. TTY server (no dependencies, but after disk)
4. PM server (no dependencies)
5. VFS server (depends on TFS)
6. Init (depends on VFS)

Each server calls `rs_ready()` after initialization to notify
the RS thread. RS blocks until the notification arrives, then
starts the next server.

    module oskit.servers

    import oskit.services.{thread_id, putc, putstr, notify_send_to, notify_read_self, rs_set_tid, svc_vm_create_server_pt, svc_vm_copy_to, svc_create_proc_susp, svc_resume_proc, svc_phys_read, svc_port_transfer, svc_proc_main_tid, svc_set_priv, svc_set_ipc_mask, svc_set_rs_tid_self, svc_get_ramdisk_base, svc_get_ramdisk_size, svc_getinfo, GETINFO_BOOT_INFO}
    import oskit.ipc.{ipc_recv_notify, port_create, port_lookup}
    import oskit.hal.memset
    import oskit.arch.{SRV_USP, SRV_SSP}

Server tracking. PIDs and MMIO page grants for each server
in boot order (0=disk, 1=tfs, 2=tty, 3=pm, 4=vfs, 5=ds,
6=nic, 7=inet, 8=unix, 9=init). Used by crash recovery to
restart a dead server.

    val RS_TOTAL_SERVERS = 10
    var rs_server_pids: [10]int
    var rs_server_io_page: [10]int
    var rs_server_ports: [10]int

Syscall privilege masks. Each server gets a bitmask (lo=bits 0-63,
hi=bits 64-95) specifying which syscalls it may call. The kernel
checks this before dispatching slow-path syscalls.

Common bits (lo): sleep(0), putc(1), yield(2), exit(3), join(4),
  thread_id(5), uptime(6), tls_set(21), tls_get(22),
  notify_send(23), notify_wait(24), notify_read(25),
  event_wait(26), event_set(27), event_clear(28),
  pimutex_lock(29), pimutex_unlock(30),
  port_create(31), ipc_send(32), ipc_recv(33), ipc_reply(34),
  port_close(35), port_register(36), port_lookup(37),
  ipc_send_timed(38), ipc_recv_notify(39), waitpid(40),
  getpid(41), thread_pid(42), thread_name_len(43), getuid(61)

    val PRIV_COMMON_LO: i64 = i64(0x7F) | (i64(7) << 21) | (i64(0xFFFFFFFF) << 24) | (i64(1) << 61)

Common bits (hi): ipc_last_msg_len(65), grant_create(71),
grant_revoke(72), sys_getinfo(77), puts(79).

sys_getinfo(77) replaces the old INFO_PAGE_VA scratch page —
every server queries its RS TID + ramdisk info at startup via
this syscall. puts(79) is the bulk-write companion to putc(1)
in PRIV_COMMON_LO — any server that can print a character can
print a buffer.

    val PRIV_COMMON_HI: i64 = i64(0x182) | (i64(1) << 13) | (i64(1) << 18)

PM extra bits (lo): vm_create_pt(44), create_proc_susp(45),
  resume_proc(46), reap_proc(47), kill_proc(48), register_pm(49),
  set_thread_ptbr(50), vm_set_ptbr(51), get_thread_pid(52),
  get_thread_ptbr(53), vm_copy_to(54), vm_copy_from(55),
  proc_state(56), proc_exit_code(57), proc_main_tid(58),
  proc_parent_tid(59), proc_set_parent_tid(60), setuid(62)

    val PRIV_PM_EXTRA_LO: i64 = i64(0x5FFFF00000000000)

TTY extra bits: kbhit(11), getkey(12), kb_set_notify(64)

    val PRIV_TTY_EXTRA_LO: i64 = i64(1) << 11 | i64(1) << 12
    val PRIV_TTY_EXTRA_HI: i64 = i64(1)

Disk extra bits: vm_v2p(66) for DMA

    val PRIV_DISK_EXTRA_HI: i64 = i64(1) << 2

Per-server privilege assignment. Called after each server is
created but before it is resumed.

    rs_set_server_priv(pid: int, idx: int)
        var lo: i64 = PRIV_COMMON_LO
        var hi: i64 = PRIV_COMMON_HI
        // IPC mask set to 0xFFFF during boot (all 16 ports allowed).
        // Tightened after all servers are up via rs_set_ipc_masks().
        var ipc = 0xFFFF
        if idx == 0
            // disk: needs vm_v2p(66) for DMA
            hi = hi | i64(4)
        else if idx == 1
            // tfs: needs grant_copy(73), grant_map(74), grant_unmap(75)
            hi = hi | i64(0xE00)
        else if idx == 2
            // tty: needs kbhit(11), getkey(12), kb_set_notify(64)
            lo = lo | i64(0x1800)
            hi = hi | i64(1)
        else if idx == 3
            // pm: needs process management syscalls (44-60, 62),
            // grant_posix_range(79) to enable POSIX shim range for
            // newly-spawned ELF (musl) processes, and fd_transplant(85)
            // for PM_CMD_TRANSPLANT_FD's shim-side helper.
            lo = lo | (i64(0x5FFFF) << 44)
            hi = hi | (i64(1) << 15) | (i64(1) << 21)
        else if idx == 4
            // vfs: needs grant_copy(73), grant_map(74), grant_unmap(75)
            hi = hi | i64(0xE00)
        else if idx == 6
            // nic: needs vm_v2p(66) for virtio DMA descriptors,
            // virtio_set_notify(76) to register for device IRQ wakes,
            // and virtio_pci_info(80) so the x86 server can fetch the
            // kernel-cached BAR/cap addresses (no-op wire on aarch64).
            hi = hi | i64(4) | i64(0x1000) | (i64(1) << 16)
        else if idx == 7
            // inet: needs timer_subscribe(81) to drive TCP
            // retransmission / TIME_WAIT scans without relying on
            // incoming frames for liveness.
            hi = hi | (i64(1) << 17)
        svc_set_priv(pid, lo, hi, ipc)

Per-server IPC send mask. Single source of truth — consulted
both at boot (rs_set_ipc_masks) and after a restart
(rs_set_ipc_mask_for). A mask of 0 means the server is a pure
receiver. Servers not listed fall through to 0.

    rs_ipc_mask_for_idx(idx: int) -> int
        val disk_port = rs_server_ports[0]
        val tfs_port = rs_server_ports[1]
        val tty_port = rs_server_ports[2]
        val pm_port = rs_server_ports[3]
        val vfs_port = rs_server_ports[4]
        val nic_port = rs_server_ports[6]
        val inet_port = rs_server_ports[7]
        val unix_port = rs_server_ports[8]
        // idx 0 (disk), 5 (ds), 6 (nic) are pure receivers → 0. unix
        // (idx 8) gains a single outbound channel to inet for the
        // Phase 2B chunk 3 SCM_RIGHTS drop-on-close path: when a
        // pending_scm tuple is abandoned (close-without-drain or
        // PID_EXIT), unix calls INET_CMD_QUEUE_REF(-1) directly so
        // the inet slot's queued_refs balances. Worst-case abuse is
        // unix issuing QUEUE_REF on an unrelated slot — the inet
        // handler's in_use/range checks make that a no-op.
        if idx == 1
            // tfs: sends to disk
            return 1 << disk_port
        else if idx == 2
            // tty: sends to pm (Ctrl-C → PM_CMD_SIGINT)
            return 1 << pm_port
        else if idx == 3
            // pm: sends to vfs (fd cleanup on exit) and inet
            // (POSIX socket cleanup on exit via PID_EXIT) and unix
            // (AF_UNIX socket cleanup likewise). Missing inet/unix
            // leaves those bits clear and the helper short-circuits
            // when port_lookup fails.
            var m = 1 << vfs_port
            if inet_port >= 0
                m = m | (1 << inet_port)
            if unix_port >= 0
                m = m | (1 << unix_port)
            return m
        else if idx == 4
            // vfs: sends to tfs and tty; also to inet when the TCP
            // scheme bridge (connect("tcp:...")) routes read/write/close
            // through INET_CMD_TCP_*. Missing inet leaves the bit clear
            // and vfs_lookup_inet returns -1, short-circuiting the bridge.
            var m = (1 << tfs_port) | (1 << tty_port)
            if inet_port >= 0
                m = m | (1 << inet_port)
            return m
        else if idx == 7
            // inet: sends to nic (ARP replies, ICMP replies,
            // UDP-over-wire). Missing nic leaves the mask at 0 and
            // inet's nic IPC wrappers degrade to returning -1.
            if nic_port < 0
                return 0
            return 1 << nic_port
        else if idx == 8
            // unix: sends to inet (Phase 2B chunk 3) and vfs
            // (Phase 2B chunk 4) for SCM_RIGHTS drop-on-close —
            // INET_CMD_QUEUE_REF(-1) on abandoned TCP/UDP tuples,
            // VFS_CMD_OFT_QUEUE_REF(-1) on abandoned FILE tuples.
            // No nic / disk reach — strictly the ref-drop channels.
            var m = 0
            if inet_port >= 0
                m = m | (1 << inet_port)
            if vfs_port >= 0
                m = m | (1 << vfs_port)
            return m
        else if idx == 9
            // init: sends to pm, vfs
            return (1 << pm_port) | (1 << vfs_port)
        return 0

Tighten IPC send masks after all servers are booted and port
IDs are known.

    rs_set_ipc_masks()
        var i = 0
        while i < RS_TOTAL_SERVERS
            if rs_server_pids[i] > 0
                svc_set_ipc_mask(rs_server_pids[i], rs_ipc_mask_for_idx(i))
            i += 1

Set IPC mask for a single server by index. Used after restart
to re-tighten the mask (rs_set_server_priv sets 0xFF default).

    rs_set_ipc_mask_for(idx: int)
        svc_set_ipc_mask(rs_server_pids[idx], rs_ipc_mask_for_idx(idx))

Ramdisk info, read from info page at startup.

    var rs_ramdisk_base = 0
    var rs_ramdisk_size = 0

Boot info, copied from info page at startup.
512 bytes = 8-byte header + 21 × 24-byte module entries, room for
the 11-entry aarch64 set (user + 10 servers) with growth headroom.

    var rs_boot_info: [512]byte
    var rs_boot_info_len = 0

Module loading buffer (192 KB). Boot module TRB/ELF data
is copied here via svc_phys_read before parsing. Sized to fit
the largest server we currently link (x86 inet).

    var rs_mod_buf: [196608]byte

Boot message helpers. putc goes straight to MMIO, no TTY needed.

    rs_print(s: string)
        val p = *byte(s)
        val n = len(s)
        var i = 0
        while i < n
            putc(p[i])
            i += 1

Wait for a server to signal ready. RS creates a dummy port
so it can use ipc_recv_notify to block for notifications.

    var rs_port = -1

    rs_wait_ready()
        if rs_port < 0
            rs_port = port_create()
        // Block until notification arrives (result == -2)
        var buf: [1]byte
        val result = ipc_recv_notify(rs_port, buf, 1)
        // result == -2 means notification received
        notify_read_self()

Hardcoded boot order. Each entry has a name and length.

    var rs_boot_names: [80]byte   // 10 entries * 8 bytes each
    var rs_boot_nlen: [10]int

    rs_init_boot_order()
        // disk
        rs_boot_names[0] = 'd'; rs_boot_names[1] = 'i'; rs_boot_names[2] = 's'; rs_boot_names[3] = 'k'; rs_boot_names[4] = 0
        rs_boot_nlen[0] = 4
        // tfs
        rs_boot_names[8] = 't'; rs_boot_names[9] = 'f'; rs_boot_names[10] = 's'; rs_boot_names[11] = 0
        rs_boot_nlen[1] = 3
        // tty
        rs_boot_names[16] = 't'; rs_boot_names[17] = 't'; rs_boot_names[18] = 'y'; rs_boot_names[19] = 0
        rs_boot_nlen[2] = 3
        // pm
        rs_boot_names[24] = 'p'; rs_boot_names[25] = 'm'; rs_boot_names[26] = 0
        rs_boot_nlen[3] = 2
        // vfs
        rs_boot_names[32] = 'v'; rs_boot_names[33] = 'f'; rs_boot_names[34] = 's'; rs_boot_names[35] = 0
        rs_boot_nlen[4] = 3
        // ds
        rs_boot_names[40] = 'd'; rs_boot_names[41] = 's'; rs_boot_names[42] = 0
        rs_boot_nlen[5] = 2
        // nic
        rs_boot_names[48] = 'n'; rs_boot_names[49] = 'i'; rs_boot_names[50] = 'c'; rs_boot_names[51] = 0
        rs_boot_nlen[6] = 3
        // inet
        rs_boot_names[56] = 'i'; rs_boot_names[57] = 'n'; rs_boot_names[58] = 'e'; rs_boot_names[59] = 't'; rs_boot_names[60] = 0
        rs_boot_nlen[7] = 4
        // unix
        rs_boot_names[64] = 'u'; rs_boot_names[65] = 'n'; rs_boot_names[66] = 'i'; rs_boot_names[67] = 'x'; rs_boot_names[68] = 0
        rs_boot_nlen[8] = 4
        // init
        rs_boot_names[72] = 'i'; rs_boot_names[73] = 'n'; rs_boot_names[74] = 'i'; rs_boot_names[75] = 't'; rs_boot_names[76] = 0
        rs_boot_nlen[9] = 4

Boot info parsing. RS reads a copy of the boot info header
from its info page at 0xBF000+24.

    rs_read_u32_le(p: *byte) -> i64
        i64(p[0] & 0xff) | (i64(p[1] & 0xff) << 8) | (i64(p[2] & 0xff) << 16) | (i64(p[3] & 0xff) << 24)

    rs_read_i64_le(p: *byte) -> i64
        rs_read_u32_le(p) | (rs_read_u32_le(p + 4) << 32)

Check if boot info header is valid (magic = "SLIX").

    rs_boot_info_valid() -> bool
        if rs_boot_info[0] != byte('S')
            return false
        if rs_boot_info[1] != byte('L')
            return false
        if rs_boot_info[2] != byte('I')
            return false
        if rs_boot_info[3] != byte('X')
            return false
        true

Get boot module count from boot info header.

    rs_boot_module_count() -> int
        val p = &rs_boot_info[4]
        int(rs_read_u32_le(p))

Find a boot module by name. Returns index or -1.

    rs_find_boot_module(name: *byte, nlen: int) -> int
        val count = rs_boot_module_count()
        var i = 0
        while i < count
            val entry = &rs_boot_info[8 + i * 24]
            // Compare name (first nlen bytes, NUL-padded)
            var found = true
            var j = 0
            while j < nlen
                if j >= 8
                    break
                if entry[j] != name[j]
                    found = false
                    break
                j += 1
            if found
                // Check rest is NUL or end of name
                if nlen < 8
                    if entry[nlen] != 0
                        found = false
                if found
                    return i
            i += 1
        -1

Get a boot module's physical address and size.

    rs_boot_module_addr(idx: int) -> i64
        rs_read_i64_le(&rs_boot_info[8 + idx * 24 + 8])

    rs_boot_module_size(idx: int) -> int
        int(rs_read_i64_le(&rs_boot_info[8 + idx * 24 + 16]))

Load a TRB v1 boot module into a process address space.
Parses the TRB header from rs_mod_buf (already copied via
svc_phys_read), copies PROGBITS segments into the target
process via vm_copy_to, and zeroes NOBITS (BSS) segments.
Returns entry point or -1 on error.

    // Program USP/SSP imported from oskit.arch (target-specific)

    rs_load_trb_module(buf: *byte, buflen: int, ptbr: u64) -> i64
        if buflen < 12
            return -1
        if buf[0] != byte('T')
            return -1
        if buf[1] != byte('R')
            return -1
        if buf[2] != byte('B')
            return -1
        if buf[3] != byte(1)
            return -1

        val entry = rs_read_u32_le(buf + 4)
        val nrec = int(rs_read_u32_le(buf + 8))
        var pos = 12
        var ri = 0
        while ri < nrec
            if pos + 12 > buflen
                return -1
            val hp = buf + pos
            val org = u64(rs_read_u32_le(hp))
            val kind = int(rs_read_u32_le(hp + 4))
            val sz = int(rs_read_u32_le(hp + 8))
            pos += 12
            if kind == 0
                // PROGBITS — copy from boot module to process address space
                if pos + sz > buflen
                    return -1
                svc_vm_copy_to(ptbr, org, buf + pos, sz)
                pos += sz
            else if kind == 1
                // NOBITS (BSS) — zero fill in process address space
                rs_zero_fill_remote(ptbr, org, sz)
            else
                return -1
            ri += 1
        entry

Load an ELF64 boot module into a process address space.
Parses program headers from rs_mod_buf, copies LOAD segments
into the target process via vm_copy_to. Returns entry point
or -1 on error.

    rs_load_elf64_module(buf: *byte, buflen: int, ptbr: u64) -> i64
        if buflen < 64
            return -1
        // Check ELF magic
        if buf[0] != 0x7F
            return -1
        if buf[1] != byte('E')
            return -1
        if buf[2] != byte('L')
            return -1
        if buf[3] != byte('F')
            return -1

        val entry = rs_read_i64_le(buf + 24)
        val phoff = int(rs_read_i64_le(buf + 32))
        val phentsize = int(rs_read_u32_le(buf + 54) & 0xFFFF)
        val phnum = int(rs_read_u32_le(buf + 56) & 0xFFFF)

        var i = 0
        while i < phnum
            val ph = buf + phoff + i * phentsize
            val ptype = int(rs_read_u32_le(ph))
            if ptype == 1
                // PT_LOAD
                val offset = int(rs_read_i64_le(ph + 8))
                val vaddr = u64(rs_read_i64_le(ph + 16))
                val filesz = int(rs_read_i64_le(ph + 32))
                val memsz = int(rs_read_i64_le(ph + 40))
                if offset + filesz > buflen
                    return -1
                if filesz > 0
                    svc_vm_copy_to(ptbr, vaddr, buf + offset, filesz)
                if memsz > filesz
                    rs_zero_fill_remote(ptbr, vaddr + u64(filesz), memsz - filesz)
            i += 1
        entry

Load a flat binary boot module (no header) into a process address
space. Used on aarch64 where servers are built as raw .bin files
via `aarch64-elf-objcopy -O binary` (see
`oskit/arch/aarch64/build_servers.sh`). The binary's load address
matches the arch's server VA — for aarch64 the linker script puts
.text + .rodata + .data at SRV_USP's carve-out base, so the entry
point is just that base (we use SRV_SSP as a proxy that sits at
the same arch-specific low end of the user carve-out on aarch64).

On x86/TRISC this path isn't reached because ELF/TRB magic matches
first — flat is the final fallback.

    val FLAT_LOAD_VA: u64 = u64(0x60000000)

    rs_load_flat_module(buf: *byte, buflen: int, ptbr: u64) -> i64
        if buflen <= 0
            return -1
        svc_vm_copy_to(ptbr, FLAT_LOAD_VA, buf, buflen)
        i64(FLAT_LOAD_VA)

Zero-fill a region in another process's address space.
Uses a local zero buffer and vm_copy_to in chunks.

    rs_zero_fill_remote(ptbr: u64, addr: u64, sz: int)
        val CHUNK = 1024
        var zero_buf: [1024]byte
        memset(zero_buf, 0, CHUNK)
        var remaining = sz
        var dst = addr
        while remaining > 0
            var chunk = remaining
            if chunk > CHUNK
                chunk = CHUNK
            svc_vm_copy_to(ptbr, dst, zero_buf, chunk)
            remaining -= chunk
            dst += u64(chunk)

Start a server from a boot module: create server page table,
copy module data via svc_phys_read, load TRB/ELF binary,
create process, resume it.
io_page = MMIO page to grant (e.g. 0x800 for ramdisk).
Returns the PID on success, 0 on failure.

    rs_start_from_module(mod_idx: int, name: *byte, nlen: int, io_page: int) -> int
        val addr = rs_boot_module_addr(mod_idx)
        val sz = rs_boot_module_size(mod_idx)

        // Copy boot module data from physical memory into our buffer
        if sz > 196608
            return 0
        svc_phys_read(u64(addr), &rs_mod_buf[0], sz)
        val buf = &rs_mod_buf[0]

        // Create server page table with MMIO grant
        val ptbr = svc_vm_create_server_pt(io_page)
        if ptbr == 0
            return 0

        // Detect format and load binary into process address space.
        // ELF (x86_64) → TRB (TRISC) → flat binary (aarch64) fallback.
        var entry: i64 = -1
        if buf[0] == 0x7F
            if buf[1] == byte('E')
                entry = rs_load_elf64_module(buf, sz, ptbr)
        if entry < 0
            entry = rs_load_trb_module(buf, sz, ptbr)
        if entry < 0
            entry = rs_load_flat_module(buf, sz, ptbr)
        if entry < 0
            return 0

        // Build a minimal argc=0 System V init stack frame at the
        // bottom of the new process's user stack. Required so that
        // programs using the prog_start.s convention (which does
        // `ldr w0, [sp]` to read argc) see a valid argc=0 instead
        // of whatever happens to live at SRV_USP. Servers using
        // srv_start.s (which just `bl main`) don't read the frame
        // but it's harmless sitting there.
        //
        // Frame: argc(8) + argv NULL(8) + envp NULL(8) + AT_NULL
        // pair(16) = 40 bytes, rounded up to 48 for 16-byte SP
        // alignment. All bytes are zero.
        var rs_stack_buf: [48]byte
        memset(&rs_stack_buf[0], 0, 48)
        val child_sp = SRV_USP - 48
        svc_vm_copy_to(ptbr, u64(child_sp), &rs_stack_buf[0], 48)

        // Create process suspended — no PTBR switch needed;
        // create_process_suspended uses vm_copy_to for the stack frame
        val sname = string(name, nlen)
        val pid = svc_create_proc_susp(entry, child_sp, SRV_SSP, sname, ptbr)
        if pid < 0
            return 0

        // Server reads RS TID + ramdisk info via sys_getinfo from its
        // own wrapper at startup — no per-process info page needed.

        // Resume the process
        svc_resume_proc(pid)
        pid

RS monitoring loop. Blocks waiting for notifications from PM
about dead server processes. When a server dies, RS restarts
it from its boot module.

    rs_monitor()
        while true
            var buf: [1]byte
            ipc_recv_notify(rs_port, buf, 1)
            val dead_pid = notify_read_self()
            if dead_pid > 0
                rs_handle_crash(dead_pid)

Handle a server crash. Find which server had this PID,
restart it from the boot module, and update tracking.

    rs_handle_crash(dead_pid: int)
        // Find which server had this PID
        var srv_idx = -1
        var i = 0
        while i < RS_TOTAL_SERVERS
            if rs_server_pids[i] == dead_pid
                srv_idx = i
                break
            i += 1
        if srv_idx < 0
            return

        // Don't restart init (last in boot order)
        if srv_idx == RS_TOTAL_SERVERS - 1
            return

        val name = &rs_boot_names[srv_idx * 8]
        val nlen = rs_boot_nlen[srv_idx]
        rs_print("RS: restarting ")
        rs_print(string(name, nlen))
        rs_print("\n")

        val mod_idx = rs_find_boot_module(name, nlen)
        if mod_idx < 0
            rs_print("RS: module not found\n")
            return

        val new_pid = rs_start_from_module(mod_idx, name, nlen, rs_server_io_page[srv_idx])
        if new_pid <= 0
            rs_print("RS: restart failed\n")
            return

        // Transfer the old port to the new server's thread so clients
        // with cached port IDs keep working transparently. The server
        // hasn't run yet (RS is higher priority), so when it calls
        // port_create(), it will get this port back.
        val old_port = rs_server_ports[srv_idx]
        if old_port >= 0
            val new_tid = svc_proc_main_tid(new_pid)
            svc_port_transfer(old_port, new_tid)

        // Set privilege mask (same restrictions as initial boot)
        rs_set_server_priv(new_pid, srv_idx)

        rs_server_pids[srv_idx] = new_pid
        rs_wait_ready()

        // Re-tighten IPC mask for the restarted server
        rs_set_ipc_mask_for(srv_idx)
        rs_print("RS: ")
        rs_print(string(name, nlen))
        rs_print(" restarted ok\n")

The RS main function. Runs as the first userspace process.
Reads config from info page at 0xBF000, then starts all
servers from boot modules in order with synchronous handshake.
After boot, RS stays alive in a monitoring loop.

    val IO_PAGE_DEVICES = 0x800

Virtio-mmio page-frame-number for slot 24..31 on QEMU's virt
machine (physical 0x0a003000 = frame 0x0a003 = 0xa003). Granted
to the nic server so it can reach virtio-net at slot 31 (0xe00
bytes into the page; server VA = MMIO_SERVER_VA + 0xe00).

    val IO_PAGE_NIC_VIRT = 0xa003

    rs_main()
        rs_set_tid(thread_id())
        // Register ourselves with the kernel so system servers can
        // query our TID via sys_getinfo(GETINFO_RS_TID).
        svc_set_rs_tid_self()

        // Read ramdisk info + boot info blob from the kernel.
        // Replaces the old per-process INFO_PAGE_VA scratch page.
        rs_ramdisk_base = int(svc_get_ramdisk_base())
        rs_ramdisk_size = int(svc_get_ramdisk_size())

        val n = int(svc_getinfo(GETINFO_BOOT_INFO, &rs_boot_info[0], 512))
        if n <= 0
            rs_print("rs: sys_getinfo(BOOT_INFO) failed\n")
            return
        rs_boot_info_len = n

        rs_init_boot_order()

        rs_print("SLIX v0.0.1\nStarting servers:\n")

        if !rs_boot_info_valid()
            rs_print("ERROR: invalid boot info\n")
            return

        // Start all servers + init from boot modules.
        // Servers that need MMIO get IO_PAGE_DEVICES; others get 0.
        // nic (idx 6) is optional — x86 has no PCI BAR grants yet,
        // so x86's ramdisk omits the nic module and the slot is
        // left empty (inet's nic IPC wrappers degrade to -1).
        var i = 0
        while i < RS_TOTAL_SERVERS
            val name = &rs_boot_names[i * 8]
            val nlen = rs_boot_nlen[i]
            rs_print("  ")
            rs_print(string(name, nlen))

            val mod_idx = rs_find_boot_module(name, nlen)
            if mod_idx < 0
                if i == 6
                    rs_print(" [skipped]\n")
                    rs_server_pids[i] = 0
                    rs_server_io_page[i] = 0
                    rs_server_ports[i] = -1
                else
                    rs_print(" MISSING\n")
                    return
            else
                // Device-access grants:
                //   disk(0), tfs(1), tty(2) → IO_PAGE_DEVICES (ramdisk + UART page)
                //   nic(6) → virtio-mmio page on aarch64 (0xa003)
                //   pm(3), vfs(4), ds(5), inet(7), init(8) → no MMIO.
                var io_page = 0
                if i < 3
                    io_page = IO_PAGE_DEVICES
                else if i == 6
                    io_page = IO_PAGE_NIC_VIRT
                val pid = rs_start_from_module(mod_idx, name, nlen, io_page)
                if pid <= 0
                    rs_print(" FAILED\n")
                    return
                rs_server_pids[i] = pid
                rs_server_io_page[i] = io_page
                rs_set_server_priv(pid, i)

                rs_print(" [mod]")
                rs_wait_ready()
                // Record server's port for transparent restart.
                // VFS registers as "fs" (not "vfs") — use correct port name.
                if i == 4
                    rs_server_ports[i] = port_lookup("fs")
                else
                    rs_server_ports[i] = port_lookup(string(name, nlen))
                rs_print(" ok\n")
            i += 1

Tighten IPC masks now that all port IDs are known.

        rs_set_ipc_masks()

        // RS stays alive — monitoring loop
        rs_print("RS monitoring\n")
        rs_monitor()
